{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of Amplitude’s HTTP V2 API, so an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"send events to an Amplitude project’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/2\/httpapi"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:17AmplitudeEncoding0A12BatchEncoderV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder.swift#L74","fileName":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"modules":[{"name":"AmplitudeEncoding"}]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/init(apiKey:plan:limit:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true},{"title":"Type Aliases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/Failure"],"anchor":"Type-Aliases","generated":true},{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"],"anchor":"Type-Properties","generated":true}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which fills in the endpoint, this encoder and Amplitude’s limits:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let amplitude = try HTTPDestination.amplitude(","    apiKey: apiKey,","    region: .eu,  \/\/ or .us, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body is a JSON object of content type "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"application\/json"},{"type":"text","text":" with two members: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"api_key"},{"type":"text","text":", the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project’s API key, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"events"},{"type":"text","text":", one object per record, oldest first, with these members:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event_properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s stored properties, by name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"event_type","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"session_id"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session’s start in Unix milliseconds, the first 48 bits of its version 7 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":"; left out for a record with no session, or a session key of another version"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in whole milliseconds since 1970","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":", and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"idfv"},{"type":"text","text":" or other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"device identifier. Amplitude counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users are sessions. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":", or one a store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recovered after a relaunch, which keeps no context) is its own anonymous user, linked to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing: Amplitude rejects an event with neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":" nor a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"user_id"},{"type":"text","text":". Amplitude drops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a second copy of an event with the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert_id"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"device_id"},{"type":"text","text":", so a recovered record that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude had already stored under its session, before the app ended, is stored again. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent. Nor is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":": neither an address nor "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$remote"},{"type":"text","text":", which asks Amplitude to look the user’s location up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the request’s address."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude limits each string value to 1,024 characters; the encoder sends longer ones as they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each event also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"app_version","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ApplicationKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The version, left out when "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"device_model","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"language","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"},{"type":"text","text":", which Amplitude stores as the language’s name"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"platform","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"os_version","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OperatingSystemKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name, its name again, and its version"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name Amplitude keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for its own events, one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a value JSON can’t, one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose timestamp has no epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeEncodingError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"default, and makes none for a batch with no record it can write, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sends"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing for it. Amplitude answers a request it takes with 200, so "},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retries"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one that gets no response, a 5xx, 408 or 429, and drops one it rejects, such as with 400 or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"413. A record sent again keeps its "},{"code":"insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The bytes are the same for the same records on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every run and platform: no whitespace, object members in the order of their names’ UTF-8"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bytes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination":{"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"HTTPDestination","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httpdestination","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AmplitudeEncoding\/documentation\/AmplitudeEncoding\/AmplitudeBatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/amplitudeencoding\/amplitudebatchencoder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of Amplitude’s HTTP V2 API, so an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"send events to an Amplitude project’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/2\/httpapi"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"AmplitudeBatchEncoder","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://AmplitudeEncoding/documentation/AmplitudeEncoding/AmplitudeBatchEncoder/init(apiKey:plan:limit:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"apiKey"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"plan"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"TrackingPlan","preciseIdentifier":"s:13TrackingPlans0A4PlanV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"limit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An encoder of the events "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","te